---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const heroStats = [
  { value: '1.38B', label: 'WeChat monthly users' },
  { value: '700M', label: 'Douyin daily users' },
  { value: '300M', label: 'Xiaohongshu monthly users' },
];

const bigFive = [
  {
    id: 'wechat',
    name: 'WeChat',
    cn: '微信',
    tagline: 'The closest thing China has to an operating system',
    image: '/Images/learn-china/platforms/wechat.png',
    imageAlt: 'A smartphone showing the WeChat home screen with chat list, payment QR code and Mini-Program tiles',
    logo: '/Images/platforms/wechat-logo.svg',
    color: '#07C160',
    colorSoft: '#E4F7EB',
    accent: '#05A050',
    stat: '1.38 billion monthly active users in early 2025',
    source: 'Tencent Q1 2025 earnings report',
    paragraphs: [
      'Everyone in China uses WeChat. Most people open it dozens of times a day without thinking about it.',
      'It started as a messaging app. It is now closer to an operating system. People pay for groceries with it, book doctors, split dinner bills, order coffee and message their boss inside the same five-minute window. Cabs take it. Street vendors tape QR codes to a wall.',
      'For brands, WeChat is closer to a CRM than to social media. Companies use Official Accounts to publish and gather followers. Mini-Programs host the store, the booking page, the member club. Moments ads bring new fans in and push them to those Mini-Programs.',
      'Starbucks and McDonald\'s both run two of the most-used Mini-Programs in China, mainly for ordering, loyalty and payment. Not really for branding.',
      'People rarely discover a brand on WeChat. But once they have followed you, that is where the relationship lives.',
    ],
    role: 'Retention engine',
  },
  {
    id: 'douyin',
    name: 'Douyin',
    cn: '抖音',
    tagline: 'A storefront disguised as an entertainment app',
    image: '/Images/learn-china/platforms/douyin.png',
    imageAlt: 'A smartphone showing a Douyin livestream commerce stream with a shoppable product card overlay',
    logo: '/Images/platforms/douyin-logo.svg',
    color: '#FE2C55',
    colorSoft: '#FEE7EC',
    accent: '#000000',
    stat: '700 million daily active users, close to two hours per user per day',
    source: 'ByteDance disclosures, 2024',
    paragraphs: [
      'Douyin is the Chinese sister of TikTok. Same parent, ByteDance. Different app, different rules, different ecosystem. For most Chinese consumers under 35, time on Douyin already beats Netflix and YouTube combined.',
      'Douyin matters because it sells. People do not just watch videos here, they buy from them. A creator shows a lipstick on screen, taps a tag, and the product lands in the viewer\'s cart in seconds.',
      'Livestreams run day and night. Hosts sell everything from face cream to SUVs. Beauty groups like Estée Lauder and L\'Oréal often run their biggest single-night sales of the year on Douyin, sometimes outselling a flagship store\'s full month in a few hours.',
      'For a growing number of brands, Douyin is the single biggest sales channel they have in China.',
    ],
    role: 'Social commerce engine',
  },
  {
    id: 'rednote',
    name: 'Xiaohongshu / RED',
    cn: '小红书',
    tagline: 'Where Chinese shoppers research before they buy',
    image: '/Images/learn-china/platforms/rednote.png',
    imageAlt: 'A smartphone showing the Xiaohongshu RED grid feed with lifestyle product posts',
    logo: '/Images/platforms/rednote-logo.svg',
    color: '#FF2741',
    colorSoft: '#FFE6EA',
    accent: '#D81B33',
    stat: '~300 million monthly active users, mostly women aged 18 to 35 in Tier 1 and Tier 2 cities',
    source: 'Xiaohongshu corporate disclosures, 2024',
    paragraphs: [
      'Xiaohongshu, known in English as RED or RedNote, sits between Instagram, Pinterest and a product review forum. People come here to read what other users actually think before they buy. Skincare, restaurants, travel, baby gear. Anything that takes a little thought.',
      'The tone is the whole point. A glossy ad usually dies on the platform. A regular user posting an honest experience can sell out a product overnight. Lululemon built its Chinese fanbase on RED long before opening any physical stores.',
      'Winning here means earning trust, not buying attention. The work splits between paid partnerships with bigger creators (KOLs), a steady drip of smaller voices (KOCs), and useful content posted from the brand\'s own account.',
    ],
    role: 'Trust, seeding and in-feed sales',
  },
  {
    id: 'tmall',
    name: 'Tmall / Taobao',
    cn: '天猫 / 淘宝',
    tagline: 'The digital flagship boutique of Chinese commerce',
    image: '/Images/learn-china/platforms/tmall.png',
    imageAlt: 'A smartphone showing a Tmall flagship store with a luxury cosmetic banner and category icons',
    logo: '/Images/platforms/tmall-logo.svg',
    color: '#FF6B00',
    colorSoft: '#FFEFE0',
    accent: '#FF0036',
    stat: 'Together, Tmall and Taobao move more product per year than Amazon, Walmart and eBay combined',
    source: 'Alibaba annual disclosures, 2024',
    paragraphs: [
      'Tmall and Taobao both belong to Alibaba and run on the same backend. The difference is who is allowed to sell. Taobao is open to anyone. Tmall is reserved for verified brands and authorized distributors. Smaller by transaction count, larger by revenue, and by a wide margin the more credible storefront for any serious brand.',
      'A Tmall flagship is the closest thing in digital retail to a real-world boutique. The brand controls the visuals, the pages, the promotions, the customer data. Nike, Apple, Nestlé and Dyson all run multi-billion-RMB businesses out of theirs.',
      'For brands without a Chinese entity, Tmall Global is the cross-border path. Stock ships from a bonded warehouse outside the mainland, tax and customs rules are lighter, sales settle in RMB. Most international brands testing China start here.',
    ],
    role: 'Conversion at scale',
  },
  {
    id: 'jd',
    name: 'JD',
    cn: '京东',
    tagline: 'A department store with its own delivery trucks parked out back',
    image: '/Images/learn-china/platforms/jd.png',
    imageAlt: 'A smartphone showing a JD product detail page for a sleek laptop with a red price and add-to-cart button',
    logo: '/Images/platforms/jd-logo.webp',
    color: '#E1251B',
    colorSoft: '#FCE5E3',
    accent: '#C81E1E',
    stat: 'Same-day and next-day delivery from JD-owned warehouses, in most major cities',
    source: 'JD.com platform disclosures, 2024',
    paragraphs: [
      'JD is Alibaba\'s main rival. If Tmall feels like a shopping mall, JD feels more like a department store with its own trucks parked out back. It owns its warehouses, runs its own drivers and ships same-day in most cities. The platform is strict on counterfeits.',
      'That trust pays off in a few categories: electronics, home appliances, baby products, fresh food, premium wine and spirits. Apple, Samsung, Huawei and Xiaomi all run major operations here, often with stronger numbers than on Tmall.',
      'JD Worldwide is the cross-border version, similar to Tmall Global. For most brands, the right answer is not Tmall or JD. It is both, with JD doing the heavy lifting wherever shoppers care about speed and authenticity.',
    ],
    role: 'Trust-driven categories',
  },
];

const restOfLandscape = [
  {
    name: 'Pinduoduo',
    cn: '拼多多',
    logo: '/Images/platforms/pinduoduo-logo.svg',
    color: '#E02E24',
    body: 'Alibaba\'s third real competitor, and in several categories the biggest of the three. Built on group-buying and aggressive pricing in lower-tier cities. Its overseas arm, Temu, is now one of the fastest-growing shopping apps in the United States.',
    note: 'International brands rarely sell here directly.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Kuaishou',
    cn: '快手',
    logo: '/Images/platforms/kuaishou-logo.svg',
    color: '#FF4906',
    body: 'Douyin\'s main rival in short video and livestream commerce. Stronger in second and third-tier cities, smaller in Tier 1. A serious channel for value brands and food categories.',
    note: 'Best paired with Douyin, not instead of.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Bilibili',
    cn: '哔哩哔哩',
    logo: '/Images/platforms/bilibili-logo.svg',
    color: '#00A1D6',
    body: 'Long-form video, especially anime, gaming and youth culture. Smaller commercial pull than the big five, but close to irreplaceable for brands going after Gen Z.',
    note: 'Where Gen Z actually spends time.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Weibo',
    cn: '微博',
    logo: '/Images/platforms/weibo-logo.svg',
    color: '#E6162D',
    body: 'Closer to a Chinese Twitter. Still useful for celebrity campaigns, PR and hashtag trends. Less useful for sustained brand engagement than it once was.',
    note: 'A PR channel more than a sales one.',
  },
];

const sellMechanics = [
  {
    id: 'wechat',
    name: 'WeChat',
    cn: '微信',
    color: '#07C160',
    colorSoft: '#E4F7EB',
    accent: '#05A050',
    icon: 'bubble',
    logo: '/Images/platforms/wechat-logo.svg',
    image: '/Images/learn-china/platforms/mech-wechat.png',
    imageAlt: 'A WeChat Mini-Program store with a product grid',
    headline: 'How WeChat sells',
    body: 'Sales run through Mini-Programs. The store, the loyalty program and WeChat Pay are wired together inside the app. Traffic comes from Official Account articles, Moments ads, customer-service chats and QR codes printed on packaging or in stores.',
    points: [
      { label: 'Mini-Program store', sub: 'Native checkout inside the app' },
      { label: 'WeChat Pay', sub: 'No login, no card entry, one tap' },
      { label: 'CRM and member tiers', sub: 'Private domain, repeat purchase' },
    ],
    hotspots: [
      { top: '22%', left: '20%', label: 'Product grid' },
      { top: '52%', left: '70%', label: 'Pay button' },
      { top: '78%', left: '32%', label: 'Member tier' },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'douyin',
    name: 'Douyin',
    cn: '抖音',
    color: '#FE2C55',
    colorSoft: '#FEE7EC',
    accent: '#000000',
    icon: 'broadcast',
    logo: '/Images/platforms/douyin-logo.svg',
    image: '/Images/learn-china/platforms/mech-douyin.png',
    imageAlt: 'A Douyin storefront with a livestream product overlay',
    headline: 'How Douyin sells',
    body: 'Three channels work in parallel. Shoppable product tags inside short videos. Livestream rooms hosted by the brand or by KOLs. And the brand\'s own Douyin Store. The algorithm pushes content toward people likely to buy, not just to watch.',
    points: [
      { label: 'Shoppable video tags', sub: 'Tag a product mid-scroll' },
      { label: 'Brand and KOL livestream', sub: 'Hours of dwell time per night' },
      { label: 'Douyin Store', sub: 'A flagship that lives in the feed' },
    ],
    hotspots: [
      { top: '20%', left: '18%', label: 'Live badge' },
      { top: '55%', left: '78%', label: 'Action stack' },
      { top: '82%', left: '50%', label: 'Buy now card' },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'red',
    name: 'RED',
    cn: '小红书',
    color: '#FF2741',
    colorSoft: '#FFE6EA',
    accent: '#D81B33',
    icon: 'heart',
    logo: '/Images/platforms/rednote-logo.svg',
    image: '/Images/learn-china/platforms/mech-red.png',
    imageAlt: 'A Xiaohongshu RED storefront with lifestyle product cards',
    headline: 'How RED sells',
    body: 'For years, RED drove discovery and Tmall captured the sale. That is changing. Brands can now open a store inside the app and sell directly, with checkout built into the feed. Livestream is smaller than on Douyin, more personal in tone.',
    points: [
      { label: 'In-feed checkout', sub: 'From post to purchase, one tap' },
      { label: 'KOC and KOL seeding', sub: 'Tiered creator program' },
      { label: 'Closing the Tmall gap', sub: 'Discovery and sale, same app' },
    ],
    hotspots: [
      { top: '24%', left: '30%', label: 'Brand banner' },
      { top: '55%', left: '70%', label: 'Product card' },
      { top: '80%', left: '24%', label: 'Heart save' },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'tmall',
    name: 'Tmall',
    cn: '天猫',
    color: '#FF6B00',
    colorSoft: '#FFEFE0',
    accent: '#FF0036',
    icon: 'store',
    logo: '/Images/platforms/tmall-logo.svg',
    image: '/Images/learn-china/platforms/mech-tmall.png',
    imageAlt: 'A Tmall flagship store homepage with product cards',
    headline: 'How Tmall sells',
    body: 'A flagship store gives the brand full control over visuals, pages, promotions and customer data. Traffic comes from in-app search, category pages, Alibaba\'s recommendation engine and paid placements via Alimama. June 18 and November 11 can deliver a year of revenue in a week.',
    points: [
      { label: 'Brand flagship store', sub: 'Visual control, data ownership' },
      { label: 'Search and category', sub: 'Buyer-intent traffic' },
      { label: '6.18 and 11.11', sub: 'Festival peaks worth a year' },
    ],
    hotspots: [
      { top: '20%', left: '50%', label: 'Hero banner' },
      { top: '50%', left: '24%', label: 'Categories' },
      { top: '78%', left: '70%', label: 'Cart' },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'jd',
    name: 'JD',
    cn: '京东',
    color: '#E1251B',
    colorSoft: '#FCE5E3',
    accent: '#C81E1E',
    icon: 'truck',
    logo: '/Images/platforms/jd-logo.webp',
    image: '/Images/learn-china/platforms/mech-jd.png',
    imageAlt: 'A JD product page with trust badges and a red add-to-cart button',
    headline: 'How JD sells',
    body: 'Same flagship logic as Tmall, but with the logistics edge. Orders ship from JD\'s own warehouses, often within hours. Same-day delivery and counterfeit policing make a real difference in high-ticket and fresh categories.',
    points: [
      { label: 'JD flagship', sub: 'Trust-first storefront' },
      { label: 'Self-run logistics', sub: 'Same-day in most cities' },
      { label: '6.18 anchor festival', sub: 'JD\'s home turf' },
    ],
    hotspots: [
      { top: '24%', left: '50%', label: 'Hero photo' },
      { top: '52%', left: '24%', label: 'Trust badges' },
      { top: '86%', left: '50%', label: 'Buy now' },
    ],
  },
];

const journey = [
  {
    phase: 'Discovery and demand',
    icon: 'spark',
    title: 'Douyin and RED build the audience',
    body: 'Short video, livestream and creator content put the brand in front of people who were not yet looking for it. RED earns the trust that makes them ready to act.',
    platforms: 'Douyin · RED',
  },
  {
    phase: 'Conversion (social and marketplace)',
    icon: 'store',
    title: 'Sales close on every channel, not just on marketplaces',
    body: 'Tmall and JD remain the home of festivals, category authority and scale. But Douyin livestreams and RED in-feed checkout convert directly inside the social apps. The winning brands let buyers transact wherever they happen to be ready.',
    platforms: 'Tmall · JD · Douyin Shop · RED Store',
  },
  {
    phase: 'Retention and loyalty',
    icon: 'bubble',
    title: 'WeChat keeps them coming back',
    body: 'Once the first purchase is in, WeChat is where the relationship lives. Mini-Programs, loyalty tiers, WeCom one-to-one chats and Moments ads turn one-off buyers into a repeat audience.',
    platforms: 'WeChat · WeCom',
  },
];

const icons: Record<string, string> = {
  bubble: `<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 12a8 8 0 0 1-12 7l-5 1 1-4a8 8 0 1 1 16-4z"/><circle cx="9" cy="12" r=".75" fill="currentColor"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r=".75" fill="currentColor"/><circle cx="15" cy="12" r=".75" fill="currentColor"/></svg>`,
  broadcast: `<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/><path d="M16.5 7.5a6 6 0 0 1 0 9M7.5 7.5a6 6 0 0 0 0 9"/><path d="M19.5 4.5a10 10 0 0 1 0 15M4.5 4.5a10 10 0 0 0 0 15"/></svg>`,
  heart: `<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20.8 8.6a5 5 0 0 0-8.8-3.2 5 5 0 0 0-8.8 3.2c0 5.6 8.8 11 8.8 11s8.8-5.4 8.8-11z"/></svg>`,
  store: `<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 9 5 4h14l1 5"/><path d="M5 9v11h14V9"/><path d="M9 20v-6h6v6"/><path d="M4 9h16"/></svg>`,
  truck: `<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 7h12v9H2z"/><path d="M14 10h4l3 3v3h-7z"/><circle cx="7" cy="18" r="2"/><circle cx="17" cy="18" r="2"/></svg>`,
  spark: `<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3v4M12 17v4M3 12h4M17 12h4M6 6l3 3M15 15l3 3M18 6l-3 3M9 15l-3 3"/></svg>`,
  quote: `<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 17q-2 0-2-2v-3q0-3 3-5l1 1q-2 1-2 3h2v6zM16 17q-2 0-2-2v-3q0-3 3-5l1 1q-2 1-2 3h2v6z"/></svg>`,
};
---

<Layout
  title="China Digital Platforms Explained for Brands | TheChinaPath"
  description="WeChat, Douyin, RED, Tmall, JD. A guide to the platforms shaping how brands reach Chinese consumers, and what each one is actually for."
>
  <div class="lcp-progress" aria-hidden="true"><div class="lcp-progress__bar"></div></div>
  <article class="lcp">

    {/* ---------- HERO ---------- */}
    <section class="lcp-hero" data-hero>
      <div class="lcp-hero__bg" aria-hidden="true" data-parallax>
        <img src="/Images/learn-china/platforms/hero-douyin-viewer.png" alt="A young woman watching a Douyin livestream on her phone, alone in a lived-in apartment" />
      </div>
      <div class="lcp-hero__overlay" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="lcp-hero__grain" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <div class="container lcp-hero__inner">
        <nav class="lcp-hero__crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/">Home</a>
          <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
          <a href="/learn-china">Learn China</a>
        </nav>
        <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--on-dark lcp-reveal">China platforms</span>
        <h1 class="lcp-hero__title lcp-reveal" style="--reveal-delay: 80ms;">
          <span class="lcp-hero__title-row">The apps that run</span>
          <span class="lcp-hero__title-row lcp-hero__title-row--highlight">China's internet.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="lcp-hero__lead lcp-reveal" style="--reveal-delay: 200ms;">
          A guide to the five platforms shaping how brands reach Chinese consumers,
          and what each one is actually for.
        </p>
        <div class="lcp-hero__actions lcp-reveal" style="--reveal-delay: 280ms;">
          <a href="/contact" class="btn btn--primary lcp-magnetic">Talk to us</a>
          <a href="#big-five" class="btn btn--ghost-light lcp-magnetic">See the big five</a>
        </div>

        <div class="lcp-hero__meta lcp-reveal" style="--reveal-delay: 360ms;">
          {heroStats.map((s) => (
            <div class="lcp-hero__meta-item">
              <span class="lcp-hero__meta-num">{s.value}</span>
              <span class="lcp-hero__meta-label">{s.label}</span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>

      <a href="#big-five" class="lcp-hero__scroll" aria-label="Scroll to next section">
        <span class="lcp-hero__scroll-line"></span>
        <span class="lcp-hero__scroll-text">Scroll</span>
      </a>
    </section>

    {/* ---------- BIG FIVE INTRO ---------- */}
    <section id="big-five" class="section lcp-bigfive-intro">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="section-header section-header--center lcp-reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">The big five</span>
          <h2>WeChat, Douyin, RED, Tmall, JD</h2>
          <p class="section-header__lead">
            Five platforms cover most of what a brand needs to do in China.
            Each one solves a different problem. Most working strategies use several at once.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="lcp-quickbar lcp-reveal">
          {bigFive.map((p) => (
            <a href={`#${p.id}`} class="lcp-quickbar__item" style={`--brand: ${p.color}; --brand-soft: ${p.colorSoft};`}>
              <span class="lcp-quickbar__logo" aria-hidden="true">
                <img src={p.logo} alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              </span>
              <div class="lcp-quickbar__text">
                <span class="lcp-quickbar__name">{p.name}</span>
                <span class="lcp-quickbar__cn">{p.cn}</span>
                <span class="lcp-quickbar__role">{p.role}</span>
              </div>
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* ---------- PLATFORM DEEP DIVES ---------- */}
    {bigFive.map((p, i) => (
      <section
        id={p.id}
        class={`section lcp-spot${i % 2 === 1 ? ' lcp-spot--reverse' : ''}${i % 2 === 1 ? ' section--alt' : ''}`}
        style={`--brand: ${p.color}; --brand-soft: ${p.colorSoft}; --brand-accent: ${p.accent};`}
      >
        <div class="container">
          <div class="lcp-spot__grid">
            <div class="lcp-spot__media lcp-reveal">
              <div class="lcp-spot__media-frame">
                <div class="lcp-spot__phone" data-tilt-target>
                  <span class="lcp-spot__phone-notch" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <span class="lcp-spot__phone-home" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <div class="lcp-spot__phone-screen">
                    <img class="lcp-spot__media-img" src={p.image} alt={p.imageAlt} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="lcp-spot__nameplate" aria-hidden="true">
                  <div class="lcp-spot__nameplate-logo">
                    <img src={p.logo} alt="" />
                  </div>
                  <div class="lcp-spot__nameplate-text">
                    <span class="lcp-spot__nameplate-en">{p.name}</span>
                    <span class="lcp-spot__nameplate-cn">{p.cn}</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="lcp-spot__body lcp-reveal" style="--reveal-delay: 120ms;">
              <span class="lcp-spot__eyebrow">
                <span class="lcp-spot__eyebrow-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                {p.name} · <span class="lcp-spot__eyebrow-cn">{p.cn}</span>
              </span>
              <h2 class="lcp-spot__title">{p.tagline}</h2>

              <div class="lcp-spot__copy">
                {p.paragraphs.map((para) => (
                  <p>{para}</p>
                ))}
              </div>

              <figure class="lcp-spot__stat">
                <span class="lcp-spot__stat-icon" aria-hidden="true" set:html={icons.quote} />
                <div>
                  <blockquote class="lcp-spot__stat-quote">{p.stat}</blockquote>
                  <figcaption class="lcp-spot__stat-source">Source: {p.source}.</figcaption>
                </div>
              </figure>

              <span class="lcp-spot__tag">Role in your mix: {p.role}</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    ))}

    {/* ---------- REST OF THE LANDSCAPE ---------- */}
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="section-header section-header--center lcp-reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">And the rest</span>
          <h2>Four more that matter, depending on what you sell</h2>
          <p class="section-header__lead">
            Five platforms do not quite tell the whole story. A few others can move the needle
            in specific categories or stages.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="lcp-rest">
          {restOfLandscape.map((r, i) => (
            <article class="lcp-rest__card lcp-reveal" style={`--brand: ${r.color}; --reveal-delay: ${i * 80}ms;`}>
              <div class="lcp-rest__head">
                <div class="lcp-rest__logo">
                  <img src={r.logo} alt={`${r.name} logo`} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
                <span class="lcp-rest__cn" aria-hidden="true">{r.cn}</span>
              </div>
              <h3 class="lcp-rest__name">{r.name}</h3>
              <p class="lcp-rest__body">{r.body}</p>
